                        "entry_id": "3173dab4-07d9-3f25-ae9b-50b89484c99f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The use of small areas of color to construct an image, based on theories of the colors' interaction in the perception of a viewer."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ce4df358-8bf5-4fe5-8865-9fe622142b97",
                                "sense_id": "24c00b97-b35d-3682-872b-f9a022943504",
                                "text": "The method, variously called pointillism, divisionism (separated colours) or neoimpressionism, is especially effective in the half-dozen monumental paintings Seurat considered his toiles de lutte (battle-canvases)."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5203ea36-9b2e-3c67-a57f-47b89c9bcbbe",
                        "entry_id": "3173dab4-07d9-3f25-ae9b-50b89484c99f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Support for division of a territory, etc."
